--- a/docs/api.md
+++ b/docs/api.md
@@ -422,9 +422,32 @@ later card had already earned can disappear.
 
 ### `GET /players/:playerId/record?asOf=YYYY-MM-DD`
 `asOf` is required. Answers `playerId`, `clubId`, `asOf`, `cards`, `yellows`, `reds`, `points`,
-`finesPence`, `matchesBanned`, `standing`.
+`finesPence`, `matchesBanned`, `matchesServed`, `matchesOutstanding`, `standing`.
 
-`standing` is `suspended` when anything is being served, `warned` from 3 points, else `clear`.
+`standing` is `suspended` while any match is outstanding as of `asOf`, `warned` from 3 points,
+else `clear`.
+
+### `GET /players/:playerId/suspensions?asOf=YYYY-MM-DD`
+`asOf` is required. Answers `playerId`, `asOf`, `matchesBanned`, `matchesServed`,
+`matchesOutstanding`, `suspended`, and `entries` (oldest first).
+
+Each entry carries `cardId`, `fixtureId`, `teamId`, `shownOn`, `matches`, `served`,
+`outstanding`, `servedIn` (fixture ids in order), and `clearedOn` (the day the last match was
+served, or `null` while any remain).
+
+Only cards that carry a ban (straight or accumulated, whichever is longer) appear in `entries`.
+A ban is served over played games of the side the card was shown for; awarded, postponed, and
+abandoned games serve nothing. Each played game serves one match off the earliest outstanding
+card shown to that side before it. Rescinded cards drop out and games they used fall through to
+later cards.
+
+### `GET /fixtures/:fixtureId/eligibility`
+Reads the day before the game. Answers `fixtureId`, `playedOn`, `asOf`, and `ineligible`:
+every registered player at either club with a match outstanding that day, home side first then
+by player id. Each entry carries `playerId`, `clubId`, `teamId` (their side in this game), and
+`outstanding`.
+
+Both routes need a bearer token and take no other query field.
 
 ---
 
